./used_binaries.at:34: $COBC --help
stdout:
cobc-rs -- a cobc-shaped compatibility driver for the gnucobol-rs interpreter

Usage: cobc-rs [options] <source.cob>

Modes:
  -x                    build a launch artifact (launcher + manifest; NOT a native executable)
  -m                    build a loadable-module launch artifact (run via `cobcrun <name>`)
  -fsyntax-only         parse + check only (no execution, no artifacts)
  -E                    preprocess-only (define/copy expansion with #line headers)
  -M [-MF file] [-MT t] make-style dependency output

Options:
  -std=<name>           dialect (default|ibm|mf|mvs|cobol85|cobol2002|cobol2014|...)
  -conf=<file.conf>     dialect configuration file
  -free | -fixed | -fformat=<fmt>   source format
  -I <dir>              copybook search path (repeatable)
  -D<NAME>[=value]      conditional-compilation define
  -o <path>             output artifact path
  --compat=strict|gnucobol-testsuite   option policy
  --print-capabilities  list supported/translated/ignored/rejected options
  --explain-translation <opts...>     explain each option's policy
  --dump-invocation-json <path>       write the structured invocation record
  --version | --info | --dumpversion | --runtime-conf | --help

The candidate is an interpreter: it emits launch manifests, never native code.
